        "Note",
        '<strong>Jerusalem captured.</strong> What Joshua 15:63 admitted Israel had failed to do, David finally accomplishes. Jerusalem becomes the City of David — politically neutral (between Judah and the northern tribes), militarily defensible, and (after the Ark’s arrival in ch 6 and Solomon’s temple in 1 Kgs 6) cosmically central. Recent excavation in the City of David (Eilat Mazar’s "Large Stone Structure") has produced a candidate for David’s palace, though identification remains debated. The conquest of Jerusalem is the foundational event of biblical Israel in its biblical form.',
