        "",
        "Michal the daughter of Saul had no child",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Michal’s end.</strong> The narrator’s terse closing of Saul’s line through Michal. Whether her childlessness is divine judgment (for despising David’s worship), David’s subsequent neglect, or simply biological is unstated. Her arc — from love of David (1 Sam 18:20) through political marriage and dynastic instrumentality back to her father’s house and now to silence — is one of the bleakest in the Davidic narrative. The text places her on the human cost of the regime change it celebrates.",
        "User original",
