        "",
        "Yahweh’s anger burned against Israel",
        "source",
        "Variant",
        "Variant",
        "<strong>Yahweh / Satan inciter variant.</strong> 2 Sam 24:1 says Yahweh incited David to take a census. 1 Chr 21:1 — telling the same story — says <em>Satan</em> incited David. The shift is one of the clearest cases of inner-biblical theological development: by the post-exilic Chronicler’s era, Israelite theology had begun to attribute morally problematic causation to a distinct adversary figure rather than directly to God. The two verses, read together, document a stage in the emergence of the Satan figure in Jewish thought — from the courtroom-accuser of Job 1–2 to the more fully developed antagonist of later apocalyptic literature.",
        "User original",
