        """<strong>M’karker (<em>מְכַרְכֵּר</em>).</strong> A rare verb suggesting whirling or leaping — David’s ecstatic dance before the ark. The cult-political stakes are high: the king of Israel publicly performs a non-royal posture, so much so that his wife Michal scorns him from the window. David’s reply ("I will be even more undignified than this") frames worship as the king’s self-emptying — proto-Pauline kenosis (Phil 2:7).""",
