        """<strong>The Davidic covenant.</strong> One of the foundational covenant passages in scripture. The promise of an eternal house, a son who will build the Temple, and a father-son bond between God and the king. Hebrews 1:5 cites this verse Christologically: applied to Christ rather than Solomon. Psalm 2:7 ("you are my son; today I have begotten you") draws on the same covenantal formula. The Davidic covenant is the messianic backbone of both Testaments.""",
