        """<strong>Nathan’s confrontation.</strong> One of the great prophetic confrontations of scripture. Nathan tells David a story about a rich man stealing a poor man’s lamb; David’s righteous anger at the parable is then turned on himself. "You are the man." The episode demonstrates the prophetic strategy of indirection — getting past defenses by storytelling. Christian preaching and pastoral practice still draw on Nathan as the model for confronting power.""",
